Shares the BMDS desktop with VNC viewers: TigerVNC, TurboVNC, noVNC, RealVNC.

Flat parts of the screen and text go losslessly (fills, palettes, zlib); pictures, video and
games go through the board's hardware JPEG encoder. Keys, the mouse and the wheel come back.

It listens on the board's own loopback: reach it through SSH,
    ssh -L 5900:localhost:5900 board
then point a viewer at localhost:5900. Set a password with 'vncserver passwd'. With the setting
vnc/listen at lan (and a password) it listens on the network too, but VNC isn't encrypted there:
the tunnel is the safer way. Start it with
'vncserver' (from autoexec.sh, or over SSH); 'vncserver stop' ends it. While it runs it has an
icon in the tray, and a viewer coming or going shows a notification.

The program must be named in the setting gui/shell-clients (Settings > Desktop) to see the
screen and type into it.
